  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-IDN151</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effective industrial relations to improve working conditions, labour productivity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite challenges in national-level social dialogue following the adoption of the Employment Creation Law and its implementing regulations since 2020, social partners in key sectors, including palm oil, fisheries, garments, and more recently energy transition, have demonstrated that constructive bipartite and tripartite dialogue can deliver tangible results. These sectoral experiences show that when employers&apos; and workers&apos; organizations engage in meaningful social dialogue, including collective bargaining, they are able to resolve disputes, anticipate change, and agree on practical solutions that balance competitiveness with workers&apos; rights.
There is growing recognition among constituents that collaborative industrial relations are essential to improving workers&#x2019; welfare, strengthening business sustainability, and enhancing labour productivity. Effective dialogue fosters mutual trust, reduces conflict, improves compliance with labour standards, and supports enterprises in adapting to evolving business models, technological change, and shifting market demands. In doing so, it contributes directly to stable industrial relations, resilient enterprises, and quality employment.
Through targeted technical support, capacity building, and the promotion of evidence-based and inclusive social dialogue processes, the ILO supports constituents in developing durable, negotiated solutions to current and emerging labour market challenges. These efforts aim to build effective industrial relations systems that advance decent work, safeguard workers&apos; welfare, improve enterprise performance, and contribute to inclusive and sustainable economic growth.</narrative>
  </description>
